{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Zero E2E tests and dozens of flaky E2E tests can both let the same critical bug reach production — what matters is having at least one E2E test a red result actually means something on.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Give each genuinely critical path (signup, checkout, core conversion) exactly one E2E smoke, and push edge cases and alternate flows down to faster, more deterministic unit and integration tests instead.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Protect a smoke test's credibility with policy as much as code — never silently retry a failure into green, and audit the E2E suite periodically for tests tracking feature count instead of real criticality.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
